# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 11-testing-quality

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- This projection attaches when production engine, app, desktop, iOS, or verify surfaces change — not only when a test file is open. Apply the APP-TEST-* GATEs to the behavior change, then add or update tests before handoff.
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

TESTING AND QUALITY (APP-TEST-\*) — EVERY APP

\================================================================================



APP-TEST-UNIT [GATE]

\- Critical business logic, calculations, validation,
transformations, and state transitions must have

  automated unit
tests appropriate to their risk.



APP-TEST-INTEGRATION [GATE]

\- Critical interactions between engine components,
persistence, vault/security storage, import/export,

  and migrations
must have automated integration coverage.



APP-TEST-UI-CRITICAL [GATE]

\- Critical user workflows must have repeatable UI
tests or documented equivalent verification, including

  Save,
Back/Cancel, validation, recovery, and core task completion.



APP-TEST-RECOVERY [GATE]

\- Critical data stores must be tested for interrupted
writes, corrupt data, unsupported versions,

  failed
migrations, and application restart after abnormal termination.



APP-TEST-OFFLINE [GATE]

\- Core workflows designated as offline-capable must be
tested with network access unavailable, including

  verification
that user work is not lost.



APP-TEST-REGRESSION [GATE]

\- Every release must run the applicable regression
suite. A release-blocking test failure must be

  resolved or
formally covered by an approved override before release.



APP-TEST-FRESH-UPGRADE [QA]

\- Before release, verify both a clean installation and
an upgrade from at least the immediately preceding

  supported
production version.



APP-TEST-REAL-DATA-SAFETY [QA]

\- Test procedures must distinguish disposable test
data from real customer/business data.

\- Test automation must not transmit or expose real
business data.

## Rule-ID coverage

Primary attachment for: APP-TEST-FRESH-UPGRADE, APP-TEST-INTEGRATION, APP-TEST-OFFLINE, APP-TEST-REAL-DATA-SAFETY, APP-TEST-RECOVERY, APP-TEST-REGRESSION, APP-TEST-UI-CRITICAL, APP-TEST-UNIT.
